sive overview of <strong>Non-Terrestrial Networks (NTNs)</strong> and the evolution of <strong>3GPP standards</strong> from 5G to 6G satellite communications. <strong>Technical whitepapers and academic studies</strong> detail how standard 5G waveforms must adapt to severe orbital challenges, including high latency, Doppler shifts, and precise timing requirements managed through device-side <strong>GNSS integration</strong>. Industry analyses highlight the transition from early <strong>transparent payloads</strong> to <strong>regenerative payloads</strong> with on-board base stations in Release 19, enabling advanced features like store-and-forward capabilities. Furthermore, market reports map the commercial landscapeâ€”contrasting standardized <strong>Mobile Satellite Service (MSS) bands</strong> with newly regulated <strong>Supplemental Coverage from Space (SCS)</strong> frameworks used by major satellite and mobile operators. Finally, research into <strong>beyond-OFDM waveforms</strong> such as AFDM and OTFS illustrates ongoing physical layer preparations for future <strong>6G space communications</strong>.</p></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></span><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c2880120021="" class="chat-panel-empty-state-action-bar"><nb-button _ngcontent-ng-c2880120021="" tabindex="-1" size="small" icon="keep_pin" class="pin-button pin-button-extended has-icon nb-button nb-button-size-small nb-button-type-outlined nb-button-badge-size-small" _nghost-ng-c2984037200="" jslog="248156;track:generic_click,impression"><!----><!----><button _ngcontent-ng-c2984037200="" type="button" matbadgeposition="after" class="mdc-button mat-mdc-button-base mat-badge mdc-button--outlined mat-mdc-outlined-button mat-unthemed mat-badge-overlap mat-badge-above mat-badge-after mat-badge-small mat-badge-hidden" mat-ripple-loader-uninitialized="" mat-ripple-loader-class-name="mat-mdc-button-ripple" aria-label=""><span class="mat-mdc-button-persistent-ripple mdc-button__ripple">